# Environment for running the wizard inside the aisc platform (compose merge).\n# Hosts are compose SERVICE NAMES on the shared `backend` network. For standalone\n# dev, set these in your shell or a local .env instead (see .env.example).\n\n# Served behind Caddy under /wizard. FastAPI's root_path makes the service's\n# /api/* routes resolve at /wizard/api/* so they don't collide with the aisc\n# backend's own /api/*.\nWIZARD_ROOT_PATH=/wizard\nWIZARD_PORT=8090\n\n# NOTE: the catalogue is currently a SEPARATE compose project, not an aisc\n# submodule. Point this at wherever its backend is reachable on the network\n# (a compose service name once both run on the same `backend` network).\n\n# The model is chosen in wizard.toml; LiteLLM reads the provider key matching\n# that model from the environment. Inject the real key via the platform env —\n# do NOT commit secrets here.\n# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=\n# OPENAI_API_KEY=\n\n# Serve a different control-objectives export instead of the bundled CSV.\n# WIZARD_OBJECTIVES_FILE=/path/to/ai_act_control_objectives.csv\n